  "slug": "elementary-quadratic-reciprocity-oq-01-oq-03-oq-01-oq-01-oq-01-oq-01-oq-01-oq-02-oq-02",
  "title": "The combined supplement to quadratic reciprocity (a = -2) as a Zolotarev permutation sign",
  "phase": "COMPLETED",
  "status": "completed",
  "tier": "B",
  "path": "full",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "J(-2 \\mid n) = (-1)^{(n-1)/2 + (n^2-1)/8} \\text{ for every odd } n > 0, \\text{ equal to } \\operatorname{sign}(x \\mapsto -2x \\text{ on } \\mathbb{Z}/n).",
    "plain": "Fuse the first supplement (a = -1) and second supplement (a = 2), both already proved as Zolotarev permutation signs, into the combined supplement for a = -2: its explicit (-1)^((n-1)/2 + (n^2-1)/8) power form, its mod-8 characterization (-2 is a quadratic residue iff n is 1 or 3 mod 8), and its reading as the sign of the permutation x -> -2x on Z/n.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Completes the trio of elementary supplements (a = -1, 2, -2) as Zolotarev permutation parities.",
      "Supplies the explicit power form of the -2 character chi8', which Mathlib carries only as a mod-8 case split."
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "jacobiSym_neg_two: J(-2 | n) = (-1)^((n-1)/2 + (n^2-1)/8) for odd n",
      "jacobiSym_neg_two_eq: J(-2 | n) = +1 iff n is 1 or 3 mod 8",
      "chi8'_eq_neg_one_pow: chi8' n = (-1)^((n-1)/2 + (n^2-1)/8) (new power form, absent from Mathlib)",
      "sign_neg_two: sign(x -> -2x on Z/n) = (-1)^((n-1)/2 + (n^2-1)/8)",
      "legendreSym_neg_two / neg_two_qr_iff: (-2/p) power form and -2 is a QR mod p iff p is 1 or 3 mod 8"
    ],
    "open": [],
    "goal": "Record the combined supplement a = -2 as a Zolotarev permutation sign with explicit power form and QR characterization."
  },
