  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: Combined supplement a = -2 proved in Lean 4, 0 sorries, 0 axioms. The genuinely new content is the chi8' power form and the x -> -2x permutation-sign reading; the value J(-2|n) = chi8' n is classical (Mathlib jacobiSym.at_neg_two).",
    "builtItems": [
      "jacobiSym_neg_two (ElementaryQuadraticReciprocityOQ01OQ03OQ01OQ01OQ01OQ01OQ01OQ02OQ02.lean:91): power form via jacobiSym.mul_left on -2 = (-1)*2 + pow_add",
      "jacobiSym_neg_two_eq (:102): mod-8 indicator via jacobiSym.at_neg_two + ZMod.chi8'_nat_eq_if_mod_eight",
      "chi8'_eq_neg_one_pow (:114): explicit power form of chi8', -2 analogue of chi8_eq_neg_one_pow (not in Mathlib)",
      "neg_one_pow_neg_two (:122): fused exponent value as mod-8 indicator",
      "sign_ringMulPerm_neg_two (:140) / sign_neg_two (:149): sign of x -> -2x via grandparent sign_ringMulPerm_eq_jacobiSym_odd, canonical unit -(ZMod.unitOfCoprime 2 _)",
      "legendreSym_neg_two (:167) / legendreSym_neg_two_eq (:175) / neg_two_qr_iff (:187): odd-prime specialization + QR characterization"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "a = -2 needs no new permutation computation: jacobiSym.mul_left reduces it to the sibling a = -1 and a = 2, and (-1)^a*(-1)^b = (-1)^(a+b) fuses their exponents; x -> -2x is the composite of negation and doubling.",
      "Mathlib's -2 character chi8' is only a mod-8 case split (chi8'_nat_eq_if_mod_eight); the closed power form chi8' n = (-1)^((n-1)/2 + (n^2-1)/8) is new and reusable, the chi8' counterpart of chi8_eq_neg_one_pow / ZMod.chi4_eq_neg_one_pow.",
      "The fused exponent (n-1)/2 + (n^2-1)/8 is even exactly for n = 1, 3 mod 8 (both summands even at 1, both odd at 3), recovering the classical 'when is -2 a QR' characterization as the parity of a single sum."
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [
      "Mathlib lacks the power forms of the small characters chi8/chi8' (it has only ZMod.chi4_eq_neg_one_pow); chi8_eq_neg_one_pow (sibling) and chi8'_eq_neg_one_pow (this entry) fill that gap and are upstream candidates."
    ],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Upstream chi4/chi8/chi8' power forms to Mathlib as a complete set.",
      "Assemble the three supplements with the main reciprocity law into a self-contained Zolotarev QR proof in the gallery."
    ]
